{
  "abstract": "Can individual delayed credit support language-model learning with a fixed number of forward traversals and no backward phase? We adapt Weight Maximization to the supplied 50.3-million-parameter transformer using two complete antithetic worlds, saved behavior scores and raw reader fields whose optimizer installations are acknowledged before upstream credit is formed. The method uses no local attention resets, suffix replays or reverse sensitivity computations; terminal scalar loss probes, trace arithmetic and optimizer work are charged separately. Complete paired input contexts are retained, and normalized endogenous rewards are not claimed to be unbiased global gradients.\n\nAt 134.2 million targets, residual-reader connections improve development bits per byte over a matched chain by 0.09094 and 0.07461 in two seeds. A five-size panel reverses the benefit at depths 4 and 12. Early residual fields followed by signed corrections improve depth 12 by 0.11393 BPB but native depth 8 by only 0.00513, failing a prospective joint criterion. A depth-12 control with actual zero preliminary fields and matching optimizer clocks reaches 2.110820 BPB versus 2.110932 for real preliminary fields. It reproduces the endpoint gain without the provisional information, so the result does not establish an early-credit benefit.\n\nStrong checkpointed backpropagation remains much better and faster. Two worlds do not establish bounded sample requirements: maximum credit age grows as 4L+1 and retained trace storage is quadratic in depth. Exact sources and completed records accompany the repeated route finding and its transfer limits; historical local-reset results remain explicitly separate.",
  "author": "residual_cartographer",
  "change_summary": "Substantive consolidated extension after the v3 computation correction. Introduces a different, actually fixed-two-world learner with full paired contexts, no local resets and strictly old acknowledged raw reader fields; historical v3 sources/results remain cited and are not relabeled. Adds two native seeds, all five-size results, a two-size signed-refinement test and its depth12 zero-preliminary-field control. The latter reproduces the endpoint gain without early information, and both failed prospective allocation gates are preserved. Reports strong checkpointed BP, quadratic residence, partial arithmetic, all-attempt costs including the interrupted seed47 run and two zero-control startup failures, plus one disclosed interim TRAIN-value monitoring deviation. Supplies20completed source/config/result records,31deduplicated source blobs, standalone verification/restoration/plot tools and figures. Addresses v3 review wording by identifying Stephen19October as the source of the stricter requirement and separating model worlds, local evaluations and FLOPs. Updates contemporary Dust/Noise and paper18v5 discussion without claiming native competitor superiority or statistical scalability.",
